# Framework Port Staging Gate

Before any **framework wiring or LI/LC-style port** ships to staging (LlamaIndex retrieve/hybrid/RRF, LangChain router, Docling/LI chunking swaps, modern rerank cutover, or any change that replaces hand-rolled retrieve/route/blend/embed paths), agents MUST run this gate. Do not deploy or enable staging flags until all three checks pass and are recorded in the handoff.

Applies to OpenCRE ask, OWASP agent, Librarian, and related comprehension paths on homeserver staging (`deploy/staging`). Does not replace `verifiable-goals.mdc` lint/mypy/test or `production-db-ops-safety.mdc`.

## When this gate is required

- Wiring or swapping LlamaIndex / LangChain / Docling / modern rerank into live paths
- Changing `CRE_RAG_PARITY_*` or `OWASP_CX_*` defaults that activate hybrid, LI retrieve, LC router, or fusion
- Changing CRE hub (or other) embedding **text templates** or re-embed pipelines that feed search/rerank
- Hot-patch or image deploys to staging that turn framework code paths on

Skip only for pure docs, hermetic unit tests with no staging deploy, or flag-off scaffolding that cannot run in production containers.

## Required checks (all must pass)

### 1. Behavior diff (old vs new) on the same eval set — before deploy

Measure **old path** and **new path** on the **same** fixed eval set (e.g. ask ablate `questions_abl_clean.jsonl` / designated main set; Librarian golden / live harness as appropriate).

Record at least:

| Dimension | What to compare |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Accuracy | Correct% / top-1 / family breakdown as applicable |
| Latency | Avg (and p50 if available) end-to-end |
| Routing | Intent/route distribution; misroutes (clarify/chapter/person on normative asks) |
| Blending | Fusion/RRF/hybrid ranking behavior vs hand-rolled path |

Do **not** ship to staging on “code looks equivalent.” Numbers first. Prefer local or flag-off vs flag-on on a non-production target; if staging is the only SoT, use a controlled ablate with rollback ready.

### 2. Flag defaults, router activation, search blending — explicit parity

Confirm and write down:

- Flag defaults (`OWASP_CX_*`, `CRE_RAG_PARITY_*`, aliases in `comprehension/flags.py`) match the **prior** staging path unless intentionally changed
- Router activation (e.g. `LC_ROUTER`) is not newly live merely because deps were installed or env leftovers existed — inert flags on old images must stay inert or be called out
- Search blending (hand-rolled RRF vs LlamaIndex QueryFusion / hybrid supplement) matches the prior path unless intentionally changed

Any intentional change MUST be called out in the PR/handoff (what changed, why, measured delta). Silent activation is a gate failure.

### 3. Embed text contains actual content — not just an ID

Before/after any embed-template or re-embed work:

- Sample hub (CRE) `embeddings.embeddings_content` (and analogous node content if touched)
- Verify description/prose fields contain **real text**, not an empty `description:` slot followed only by `id:…` / external id
- If `cre.description` (or source prose) was updated, confirm re-embed actually refreshed `embeddings_content` (incremental skip must not leave stale empty-description vectors)

SQL/sample evidence required in the handoff (e.g. ≥20 CRE rows where content includes description prose).

## Ship rule (staging)

Enable framework flags / cut over default paths on staging only if **accuracy and runtime are the same or better** than the recorded baseline for that eval set. Otherwise keep flags off and leave hand-rolled paths. Reference baselines from the active cre-backlog epic / latest staging ablate (e.g. ask ~67.1% / ~12.1s avg on 246 Q when that was the measured baseline).

## Handoff evidence

Report paths, commands, and numbers — not assertions alone:

```
framework-port gate — behavior diff: old A% / Xs vs new B% / Ys (eval set …)
framework-port gate — flags/router/blend: match prior | intentional change: …
framework-port gate — embed text sample: N/N rows contain description prose
framework-port gate — ship decision: keep off | enable (criteria met)
```
